From dc307c76d31696bbcbb77c624fd3d13fbc382859 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taehyun Kim <dice.thkim@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 15:09:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/28] SCUMM: Add a Korean TTF font map

Move Korean hi-res TTF face selection out of hardcoded per-option logic
and into a small INI-style map file selected by korean_ttf_map.

The map defines font roles and maps original bitmap heights to those
roles. This lets a target use a serif face for large title/credit text,
a regular sans face for normal UI text, and a bold sans face for compact
fonts that become 24px at 3x scaling.

Existing korean_ttf_font, korean_ttf_bold_font, and
korean_ttf_title_font keys remain as fallbacks, so older configs still
work without a map file.
---
 engines/scumm/charset.cpp | 146 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 engines/scumm/scumm.h     |   4 ++
 2 files changed, 123 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

diff --git a/engines/scumm/charset.cpp b/engines/scumm/charset.cpp
index 4d6eaa7d..38fef8f4 100644
